Feature description: The sigmoid transformation of the rank sum feature.\n# Usefulness: Introduces a bounded transformation that scales rank_sum into a [0, 1] range, useful for models that might be sensitive to raw magnitude differences in rank sums. \ndf['sigmoid_rank_sum'] = 1 / (1 + np.exp(-df['rank_sum']))", "# Feature name: flush_rank_spread\n# Feature description: Difference between the highest and lowest ranks in a hand, calculated only if the hand is a Flush (is_flush=True).\n# Usefulness: Helps further distinguish between simple Flush (Target=5) hands and Straight Flush (Target=8) or Royal Flush (Target=9), as the latter will have more specific rank distributions.\ndf['flush_rank_spread'] = df.apply(lambda row: max([row['V2'], row['V4'], row['V6'], row['V8'], row['V10']]) - min([row['V2'], row['V4'], row['V6'], row['V8'], row['V10']]) if row['is_flush'] else 0, axis=1)"]
