y to the rank_sum_normalized feature, which might help in capturing patterns in the target classes by emphasizing specific normalized values of rank sums.\\ndf[\'rank_sum_normalized_sine\'] = np.sin(df[\'rank_sum_normalized\'])", "# Feature name: rank_difference_std_squared\\n# Feature description: The square of the rank difference standard deviation.\\n# Usefulness: Highlights hands with significant variability in rank differences, aiding in distinguishing complex rank patterns (e.g., distinguishing Straights from non-Straights).\\ndf[\'rank_difference_std_squared\'] = df[\'rank_difference_std\']  2", "# Feature name: card_suit_match_to_std_ratio\\n# Feature description: The ratio of card_suit_match_count to rank_difference_std.\\n# Usefulness: Combines information about suit similarity and rank difference variability into a single feature, which can help differentiate combinations involving both suit and rank patterns like Flush or Straight-related hands.\\ndf[\'card_suit_match_to_std_ratio\'] = df[\'card_suit_match_count\'] / (df[\'rank_difference_std\'] + 1e-6)", "# Feature name: exp_card_rank_match_count\\n# Feature description: The exponential of the card_rank_match_count feature.\\n# Usefulness: Emphasizes the importance of rank matches exponentially. This could improve the separability for hands with extreme matches, such as Full House and Four of a Kind.\\ndf[\'exp_card_rank_match_count\'] = np.exp(df[\'card_rank_match_count\'])", "# Feature name: royal_flush_candidate_and_flush\\n# Feature description: Boolean feature indicating whether a hand is both a Royal Flush candidate and a Flush.\\n# Usefulness: A direct indicator for detecting the highest-ranking hand, Royal Flush (Target=9). Reduces complexity for the model by precomputing this condition.\\ndf[\'royal_flush_candidate_and_flush\'] = df.apply(lambda row: row[\'royal_flush_candidate\'] and row[\'is_flush\'], axis=1)", "# Feature name: tanh_rank_difference_std\\n# Feature description: The hyperbolic 