[{'["# card_suit_match_count\\n# Feature description: The number of suits that are the same across the five cards. This is useful because matching suits are critical for identifying Flush and Royal Flush hands. It simplifies detecting these patterns.\\n# Usefulness: Helps identify hands like Flush (five cards with the same suit) and contributes to detecting Straight Flush and Royal Flush. Additionally, it may help differentiate other combinations like nothing (Target=0).\\n\\ndf[\'card_suit_match_count\'] = df[[\'V1\', \'V3\', \'V5\', \'V7\', \'V9\']].apply(lambda x: len(set(x)), axis=1)", "# card_rank_match_count\\n# Feature description: The number of ranks that are the same across the five cards. This feature aids in identifying pairs, two pairs, three of a kind, full house, and four of a kind combinations.\\n# Usefulness: Directly contributes to better predictive power for combinations requiring rank matches (Target=1, 2, 3, 6, 7).\\n\\ndf[\'card_rank_match_count\'] = df[[\'V2\', \'V4\', \'V6\', \'V8\', \'V10\']].apply(lambda x: len(set(x)), axis=1)", "# rank_difference_std\\n# Feature description: The standard deviation of consecutive rank differences across the five cards. This feature helps identify Straight hands where ranks are sequential.\\n# Usefulness: Essential for detecting Target=4 (Straight), Target=8 (Straight Flush), and Target=9 (Royal Flush).\\n\\ndf[\'rank_difference_std\'] = df[[\'V2\', \'V4\', \'V6\', \'V8\', \'V10\']].apply(lambda x: np.std(np.diff(sorted(x))), axis=1)", "# is_flush\\n# Feature description: Boolean feature indicating whether all suits are the same across the five cards.\\n# Usefulness: Directly identifies Flush (Target=5) and contributes to detecting Straight Flush (Target=8) and Royal Flush (Target=9).\\n\\ndf[\'is_flush\'] = df[[\'V1\', \'V3\', \'V5\', \'V7\', \'V9\']].apply(lambda x: len(set(x)) == 1, axis=1)", "# is_straight\\n# Feature description: Boolean feature indicating whether ranks are sequential across the five cards. Allows wrap-around handling for Ace (1) being higher than King (13).\\n# Usefulness: Directly identifies Target=4 (Straight) and contributes to detecting Straight Flush and Royal Flush patterns.\\n\\ndf[\'is_straight\'] = df[[\'V2\', \'V4\', \'V6\', \'V8\', \'V10\']].apply(\\n    lambda x: sorted(x) == list(range(min(x), min(x) + 5)) or sorted(x) == [1, 10, 11, 12, 13],\\n    axis=1\\n)", "# rank_sum\\n# Feature description: The sum of all ranks across the five cards.\\n# Usefulness: Helps detect Royal Flush (Target=9) since {Ace, King, Queen, Jack, Ten} has a fixed sum (54) when ranks are sequential. May work as a secondary confirmation for certain combinations.\\n\\ndf[\'rank_sum\'] = df[[\'V2\', \'V4\', \'V6\', \'V8\', \'V10\']].sum(axis=1)", "# royal_flush_candidate\\n# Feature description: Boolean flag indicating whether the hand is a potential Royal Flush ({Ace, King, Queen, Jack, Ten}) based on ranks alone, ignoring suits.\\n# Usefulness: Narrows down potential Royal Flush candidates (Target=9), reducing noise for classification.\\n\\ndf[\'royal_flush_candidate\'] = df[[\'V2\', \'V4\', \'V6\', \'V8\', \'V10\']].apply(\\n    lambda x: set(x) == {1, 10, 11, 12, 13}, \\n    axis=1\\n)", "# drop_unnecessary_suit_features\\n# Feature description: Removing individual suit features to reduce dimensionality after creating aggregated features.\\n# Usefulness: These features have been aggregated into more meaningful representations like card_suit_match_count and is_flush.\\n\\ndf.drop(columns=[\'V1\', \'V3\', \'V5\', \'V7\', \'V9\'], inplace=True)", "# drop_unnecessary_rank_features\\n# Feature description: Removing individual rank features to reduce dimensionality after creating aggregated features.\\n# Usefulness: These features have been aggregated into more meaningful representations like card_rank_match_count, rank_difference_std, and rank_sum.\\n\\ndf.drop(columns=[\'V2\', \'V4\', \'V6\', \'V8\', \'V10\'], inplace=True)"]': 0.26265109608686754}, {'["# Featur