rds. Allows wrap-around handling for Ace (1) being higher than King (13).\\n# Usefulness: Directly identifies Target=4 (Straight) and contributes to detecting Straight Flush and Royal Flush patterns.\\n\\ndf[\'is_straight\'] = df[[\'V2\', \'V4\', \'V6\', \'V8\', \'V10\']].apply(\\n    lambda x: sorted(x) == list(range(min(x), min(x) + 5)) or sorted(x) == [1, 10, 11, 12, 13],\\n    axis=1\\n)", "# rank_sum\\n# Feature description: The sum of all ranks across the five cards.\\n# Usefulness: Helps detect Royal Flush (Target=9) since {Ace, King, Queen, Jack, Ten} has a fixed sum (54) when ranks are sequential. May work as a secondary confirmation for certain combinations.\\n\\ndf[\'rank_sum\'] = df[[\'V2\', \'V4\', \'V6\', \'V8\', \'V10\']].sum(axis=1)", "# royal_flush_candidate\\n# Feature description: Boolean flag indicating whether the hand is a potential Royal Flush ({Ace, King, Queen, Jack, Ten}) based on ranks alone, ignoring suits.\\n# Usefulness: Narrows down potential Royal Flush candidates (Target=9), reducing noise for classification.\\n\\ndf[\'royal_flush_candidate\'] = df[[\'V2\', \'V4\', \'V6\', \'V8\', \'V10\']].apply(\\n    lambda x: set(x) == {1, 10, 11, 12, 13}, \\n    axis=1\\n)", "# drop_unnecessary_suit_features\\n# Feature description: Removing individual suit features to reduce dimensionality after creating aggregated features.\\n# Usefulness: These features have been aggregated into more meaningful representations like card_suit_match_count and is_flush.\\n\\ndf.drop(columns=[\'V1\', \'V3\', \'V5\', \'V7\', \'V9\'], inplace=True)", "# drop_unnecessary_rank_features\\n# Feature description: Removing individual rank features to reduce dimensionality after creating aggregated features.\\n# Usefulness: These features have been aggregated into more meaningful representations like card_rank_match_count, rank_difference_std, and rank_sum.\\n\\ndf.drop(columns=[\'V2\', \'V4\', \'V6\', \'V8\', \'V10\'], inplace=True)"]': 0.26265109608686754}, {'["# Feature name: card_suit_match_count_squared\\n# Feature description: The square of the number of suits that are the same across the five cards.\\n# Usefulness: Squaring this feature exaggerates its importance and helps focus on hands with high suit similarity, such as Flush (Target=5), Straight Flush (Target=8), and Royal Flush (Target=9). It adds nonlinearity to distinguish between noise and patterns in suit matches.\\ndf[\'card_suit_match_count_squared\'] = df[\'card_suit_match_count\']  2", "# Feature name: log_rank_sum\\n# Feature description: The logarithm of the rank sum across the five cards.\\n# Usefulness: Introducing a logarithmic transformation smooths out the differences for very high values of rank sum (e.g., Royal Flush) versus lower-ranked hands, making the feature more interpretable and stable while aiding in distinguishing different poker hand categories.\\ndf[\'log_rank_sum\'] = np.log1p(df[\'rank_sum\'])", "# Feature name: is_high_card_flush\\n# Feature description: Boolean flag indicating whether the combination is a Flush (is_flush=True) with all ranks higher than or equal to 10.\\n# Usefulness: Filters for strong Flush combinations where all cards have high ranks, helping to better distinguish Royal Flush (Target=9) and strong Flushes (Target=5) from weaker ones.\\ndf[\'is_high_card_flush\'] = df.apply(lambda row: row[\'is_flush\'] and row[\'rank_sum\'] >= 54, axis=1)", "# Feature name: rank_sum_modulo_ten\\n# Feature description: The modulo 10 value of the rank sum across the five cards.\\n# Usefulness: This feature detects patterns or cyclic behaviors in rank_sum values that may align with specific hand types (e.g., combinations with specific remainder properties).\\ndf[\'rank_sum_modulo_ten\'] = df[\'rank_sum\'] % 10", "# Feature name: card_rank_match_count_cubed\\n# Feature description: The cube of the card_rank_match_count feature.\\n# Usefulness: Amplifies the importance of matching ranks for high-cardinality hands like Four of a Kind (Target=7) or Full House (Target=6). This non-linear feature transformation can improve separability for these combinations.\\ndf[\'card_rank_match_count_cubed\'] = df[\'card_rank_match_count\']  3", "# Feature name: rank_difference_std_inverse\\n# Feature description: The reciprocal of the rank_difference_std feature.\\n# Usefulness: Highlighting the inverse of the rank difference\'s standard deviation focuses on hands where rank_std differences are very small, such as Straights (Target=4), Straight Flushes (Target=8), or Royal Flushes (Target=9).\\ndf[\'rank_difference_std_inverse\'] = 1 / (df[\'rank_difference_std\'] + 1e-6)  # Adding epsilon to avoid division by zero", "# Feature name: straight_flush_indicator\\n# Feature description: Boolean flag indicating whether the hand is both a Straight (is_straight=True) and a Flush (is_flush=True).\\n# Usefulness: Directly detects Straight Flush (Target=8) hands, simplifying classification of one of the strongest poker hands.\\ndf[\'straight_flush_indicator\'] = df[\'is_straight\'] & df[\'is_flush\']", "# Feature name: royal_flush_vs_straight_flush\\n# Feature description: Numeric flag indicating if the hand is a Royal Flush candidate (royal_flush_candidate=True) that also satisfies Straight Flush conditions.\\n# Usefulness: Helps pinpoint Royal Flush (Target=9) from other Straight Flushes (Target=8) by combining these two key indicators.\\ndf[\'royal_flush_vs_straight_flush\'] = df.apply(lambda row: row[\'royal_flush_candidate\'] and row[\'straight_flush_indicator\'], axis=1)", "# Feature name: rank_sum_normalized\\n# Feature description: The rank sum divided by the number of cards in the hand (fixed at 5).\\n# Usefulness: Provides a normalized view of rank_sum, useful in comparing different hands on a per-card basis, aiding in differentiating lower-ranked combinations from higher-ranked ones.\\ndf[\'rank_sum_normalized\'] = df[\'rank_sum\'] / 5", "# Feature name: suit_match_to_rank_match_ratio\\n# Feature description: The ratio of card_suit_match_count to card_rank_match_count.\\n# Usefulness: Evaluates the relative importance of suit similarity versus rank similarity in identifying specific hands (e.g., Flush vs. Four of a Kind), improving model interpretability and sensitivity.\\ndf[\'suit_match_to_rank_match_ratio\'] = df[\'card_suit_match_count\'] / (df[\'card_rank_match_count\'] + 1e-6)  # Adding epsilon to avoid division by zero"]': 4.878001190200543e-06}]
