umns=[\'V2\', \'V4\', \'V6\', \'V8\', \'V10\'], inplace=True)"]': 0.0}, {'["# Feature name: card_rank_match_count_squared\\n# Feature description: The square of the card_rank_match_count feature.\\n# Usefulness: Enhances the importance of rank matches for hands involving multiple identical ranks. \\n# Expanding this feature with a quadratic form helps distinguish stronger patterns in Full House (Target=6), \\n# Four of a Kind (Target=7), and other rank-match-dependent hands.\\n\\ndf[\'card_rank_match_count_squared\'] = df[\'card_rank_match_count\']  2", "# Feature name: log_rank_sum_normalized\\n# Feature description: The logarithm of rank_sum_normalized (rank_sum divided by the number of cards in the hand).\\n# Usefulness: Combines normalization and logarithm transformation to improve model stability when handling the rank sum.\\n# Helps distinguish high-ranked hands such as Royal Flush (Target=9) from others where rank sums are distributed over a wider range. \\n\\ndf[\'log_rank_sum_normalized\'] = np.log1p(df[\'rank_sum_normalized\'])", "# Feature name: is_super_high_card_flush\\n# Feature description: A Boolean flag to detect hands where all cards are above Queen (rank >= 12) and the hand is a Flush (all suits identical).\\n# Usefulness: Fine-grained refinement of Flush (Target=5) and Royal Flush (Target=9). Helps focus on ultra-high-rank Flush hands,\\n# enabling the model to prioritize high-value patterns.\\n\\ndf[\'is_super_high_card_flush\'] = df.apply(\\n    lambda row: row[\'is_flush\'] and all(rank >= 12 for rank in [row[\'V2\'], row[\'V4\'], row[\'V6\'], row[\'V8\'], row[\'V10\']]),\\n    axis=1\\n)", "# Feature name: normalized_suit_rank_ratio\\n# Feature description: The ratio of card_suit_match_count to rank_sum_normalized. \\n# Divides the number of matching suits by the average rank per card adjusted for total rank sum. \\n# Usefulness: This captures the balance between suit similarity and rank strength. \\n# Helpful for distinguishing combinations like Flush (Target=5) versus high pairs or non-suited patterns.\\n\\ndf[\'normalized_suit_rank_ratio\'] = df[\'card_suit_match_count\'] / (df[\'rank_sum_normalized\'] + 1e-6)", "# Feature name: rank_difference_range\\n# Feature description: The range of rank differences across the cards, calculated as max(rank) - min(rank).\\n# Usefulness: Supplements rank_difference_std to support detection of sequential hands like Straight (Target=4) or Straights in combination with Flush (Targets 8 and 9). \\n# Works as a simpler range-based indication of rank spread.\\n\\ndf[\'rank_difference_range\'] = df[[\'V2\', \'V4\', \'V6\', \'V8\', \'V10\']].apply(\\n    lambda x: max(x) - min(x),\\n    axis=1\\n)", "# Feature name: log_rank_sum_modulo_bin\\n# Feature description: A binned version of the logarithm of rank_sum_modulo_ten, where the modulo operation echoes cyclic trends in the rank distribution.\\n# Usefulness: Enables detection of cyclic rank patterns and enhances signal extraction in modulo-based transformations like Straight or random Target classification.\\n\\ndf[\'log_rank_sum_modulo_bin\'] = pd.cut(\\n    np.log1p(df[\'rank_sum_modulo_ten\']),\\n    bins=5,\\n    labels=[Very Low, Low, Medium, High, Very High]\\n)", "# Feature name: zscore_rank_sum_normalized\\n# Feature description: The z-score normalization of rank_sum_normalized.\\n# Usefulness: Helps identify outliers or extreme values in rank_sum, \\n# focusing on hands like Royal Flush (Target=9) and distinguishing them from noisy distributions.\\n\\ndf[\'zscore_rank_sum_normalized\'] = (df[\'rank_sum_normalized\'] - df[\'rank_sum_normalized\'].mean()) / df[\'rank_sum_normalized\'].std()", "# Feature name: straight_flush_high_rank_flag\\n# Feature description: Boolean flag to identify Straight Flush hands where the lowest card rank is at least 10.\\n# Usefulness: Differentiates high-value Straight Flush (Target=8) combinations and enhances precision in classifying hands near Royal Flushes (Target=9).\\n\\ndf[\'